    d: "Congenital ptosis, from developmental dystrophy of the levator palpebrae superioris, characteristically shows all three signs together: an absent upper-lid crease, compensatory chin elevation, and forehead corrugation from frontalis overaction. Each sign reflects the same underlying mechanism, a weak or absent levator that the child compensates for using surrounding muscles and posture. Recognising the combination, rather than any single sign alone, is what makes the diagnosis clinically reliable.",
