    c: 'Goblet cells are genuine secretory structures (mucin), so they belong among the true parts of the secretory system, not the exception.',
    d: "The lacrimal sac is a drainage (excretory) structure, receiving tears from the canaliculi and passing them to the nasolacrimal duct; it does not itself secrete any component of the tear film. Among the lacrimal gland, accessory lacrimal glands and goblet cells, all genuinely secretory, the sac is the one structure that belongs to the drainage pathway instead. This is exactly the exception the question asks for.",
