    d: "Fluorescein angiography images the retinal and choroidal vasculature after intravenous dye injection, an entirely different investigation from the lacrimal work-up despite sharing the name fluorescein. It has no role in investigating epiphora. Among these four options it is therefore the one that is NOT part of the epiphora work-up, which is what the question asks for.",
