    d: "Contrast dacryocystography images the lacrimal drainage pathway directly after canalicular contrast injection, and all three listed uses reflect the same underlying strength. It visualises the drainage anatomy and any structural lesion within it, unlike a purely functional test such as the regurge test. Confirming an obstruction's exact site before surgery, diagnosing a diverticulum or fistula, and characterising a filling defect from a tumour or stone are therefore all genuine, simultaneous indications, which is why the correct answer combines them all.",
