    c: "Endophthalmitis, infection confined within the globe itself, does not typically produce forward displacement of the globe the way an orbital or panophthalmitic process does; it stays an intraocular problem rather than an orbital space-occupying one. Among panophthalmitis, orbital cellulitis and Graves' disease, all genuinely orbital or trans-orbital processes capable of producing proptosis, endophthalmitis is the one that is NOT a recognised cause. This is exactly the exception the question asks for.",
    d: "Graves' disease (thyroid eye disease) is a recognised cause of proptosis, so it belongs among the true causes, not the exception.",
