    d: "Thyroid eye disease causes upper LID RETRACTION, the opposite eyelid-margin change from ectropion (outward rolling of the lid margin, a separate condition with separate mechanisms such as skin shortening or age-related laxity). Ectropion is not a recognised feature of thyroid eye disease. Among diplopia, optic neuropathy and lid retraction, all genuine TED features, ectropion is the one that does NOT belong, which is exactly the exception the question asks for.",
